      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could this be forceEnableBackoff, which would be set by the caller as `queryMode \u003d\u003d AGGRESSIVE_QUERY_MODE \u0026\u0026 hasReply` ? I think it would be clearer to have the selection of what kind of scheduling to use in the caller (MdnsServiceTypeClient), as this class is pretty complicated.\n\nThen the condition would become:\n\n```\nif (mLastScheduledQueryTaskArgs \u003d\u003d null \u0026\u0026 !forceEnableBackoff) {\n   ...\n} else {\n   ...\n}\n```\n\nWhich is slightly different since there would be no backoff in aggressive mode if there was no reply from cache. That only makes a difference when resolving a service, and there\u0027s another service in cache with a different name but the same service type, so there\u0027s no reply from cache but there is a minTtl. Arguably in that case it\u0027s better not to backoff since we need to query additional results.",
